# tools/p/pond_enclosure_built_witness.rish -- what the enclosure builds, against what Pond declares.
#
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/p/pond_enclosure_built_witness.rish
#
# WHAT THIS HOLDS. Orbit two of the quest that retires ai-jail derives every grant from the
# declaration a witness reads, so the record has to name the WHOLE enclosure rather than the part a
# launcher spells. Its sibling tools/p/pond_policy_launcher_witness.rish reads the record against
# tools/ag/agent-jail.sh and says plainly in its own header that it compares what the launcher
# SPELLS. The jail supplies twenty-one more mounts from its own defaults, and until 20260828 the
# record declared six of twenty-seven. This reads `ai-jail --dry-run` -- the bwrap plan, printed
# without starting anything -- and gates the record against it at zero undeclared.
#
# WHAT THIS DOES NOT REACH. Whether the kernel honors the plan bwrap is handed, and whether a
# declaration Pond PLACES is one Pond should place. The record reads REFUSE on this pier today,
# naming `map /sys`, and that verdict is the module working rather than a fault here: this witness
# proves the record is COMPLETE, and pond_enclosure_policy_witness.rish reads what it says.
#
# ACCRETE-ONLY. This reads ai-jail's own printed plan and Pond's record. It rewrites neither, it
# starts no enclosure, and the ENCLOSURE selector stays ai-jail until the switchover round lands
# behind its audit.

say "enclosure-built: Language EN -- a record that names a fifth of the enclosure derives a fifth of an enclosure."
say "enclosure-built: Style Gauge, Meter -- each detail line names the declaration, so a count becomes a line to open."
say "enclosure-built: Lens TAME -- safety first: the plan roster is bounded, the gate is proven from both sides, and the live reading is reported rather than trusted."

let scan = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/p/pond_enclosure_built_scan.sh"]
assert scan.ok else "enclosure-built: the scan must complete -- ${scan.out}"
say scan.out
assert scan.out contains "undeclared_builds=0" else "enclosure-built: the plan must build nothing the record fails to declare"
assert scan.out contains "verdict=ok" else "enclosure-built: the seam must read ok"

let control = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/p/pond_enclosure_built_control.sh"]
assert control.ok else "enclosure-built: the control must complete -- ${control.out}"
say control.out
assert control.out contains "control_failures=0" else "enclosure-built: every planted behavior must hold"
assert control.out contains "control_verdict=ok" else "enclosure-built: the control must report ok"

say "GREEN: pond enclosure-built -- the record names every mount the plan builds, and the gate is proven from both sides."
